WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
- So good to see you again
in person, especially.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.230
But, it is amazing your reach with people.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.550
Like everybody loves you.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:06.810
And you're so inspiring.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.520
And you've inspired so many people

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.020
to do so many great projects.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.190
But speaking of in person,

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.330
Broadway is back, so-

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.629
- Broadway is back, ya'll.
- I know.

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:15.578
(crowd cheering)
It's so exciting.

00:00:15.578 --> 00:00:16.472
I know.
- Yeah.

00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:17.310
- They have to be excited.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.240
Everyone's been out of work.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.073
So there's that.

00:00:19.073 --> 00:00:19.920
But also just the creativity.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.710
I feel like that is like
the lifeline of New York.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.135
Like it's like the blood flow for me.

00:00:24.135 --> 00:00:25.080
- Yeah I feel, yeah.
- At least as a Taurus.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.000
- We're all like Tinkerbell and Peter Pan.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.590
We need applause to live.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.423
- Yeah.

00:00:29.423 --> 00:00:30.256
Yeah (Kelly and audience laughs)

00:00:30.256 --> 00:00:31.590
- And our cast members.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.050
We're waiting for a year and a half

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.340
to be back up on that stage.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.180
And, I gotta say,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.100
not only is Hamilton back.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.690
It's never been a better time

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:40.860
to see a Broadway show.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:41.693
Because,
- Yeah.

00:00:41.693 --> 00:00:42.540
- even the long running shows

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.950
have now had a rehearsal process.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.120
They had to start from scratch.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.590
And put their shows back up again.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.930
So I was at the reopening of Phantom.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.514
Yes, a couple weeks ago.

00:00:50.514 --> 00:00:51.840
- Yeah.
- And it was just like,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.190
unbelievable.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.980
- Wait, I heard that Andrew
Lloyd Webber DJ'd after.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:56.850
Did you see that?

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:57.750
- Yeah, sure.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.800
Naturally.
- Because I think

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.970
that that's amazing.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:01.442
- AL Dubs on the one and twos

00:01:01.442 --> 00:01:02.430
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:03.750
When we left the show.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.623
- And a five, six.
- Yeah, look at him.

00:01:04.623 --> 00:01:05.456
There he is.

00:01:05.456 --> 00:01:06.289
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:07.206
DJ AL Dubs.

00:01:08.696 --> 00:01:09.690
- So is it true that you-

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.680
I did this as well.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.583
Did you perform at Bar in Bat Mitzvah's?

00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:13.416
- I did.

00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:14.249
- [Kelly] I did as well.

00:01:14.249 --> 00:01:15.510
- I was, I didn't sing.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.343
I was-

00:01:16.343 --> 00:01:17.176
- Oh, I did.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.009
- I was one of the people

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:20.040
whose job it was to just encourage

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.960
kids and grandmas,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.163
and aunties to dance.
- Wait,

00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:25.193
Were you a life coach at parties?

00:01:25.193 --> 00:01:26.640
(Kelly and audience laughs)
- I was like, no.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:27.473
They'd say,

00:01:27.473 --> 00:01:29.400
"Wear a black silk shirt and black pants."

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.020
And like, "We pick you up in a van."

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.910
It was 400 bucks a gig.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.045
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Which was like my rent.

00:01:35.045 --> 00:01:35.914
- Which is amazing.
- [Lin] Yeah.

00:01:35.914 --> 00:01:37.020
- That's good money.
- And you'd go.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:37.853
And you're-

00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:38.820
And I was horrible at it.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:39.817
Because my dog would be like,

00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:41.100
"Hey Rachel, hey girls.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.187
Like, wanna dance?"

00:01:43.187 --> 00:01:44.910
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:45.743
You know?

00:01:45.743 --> 00:01:46.576
And there were guys with me

00:01:46.576 --> 00:01:47.409
who were really confident.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:48.270
Like sort of good looking

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.397
like Long Island guys who were like,

00:01:49.397 --> 00:01:50.610
"Yeah, it's really cool.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.443
You dance.

00:01:51.443 --> 00:01:52.500
Sometimes the moms give you their number.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.389
It's like really great."

00:01:53.389 --> 00:01:54.397
- Oh my gosh.
- And I was like,

00:01:54.397 --> 00:01:55.907
"I am not made for this."

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:56.740
(audience laughing)

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.560
I am too nervous and introverted.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.430
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.480
- But it was, yeah.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.770
I left the last of my dignity

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.030
in a Bar Mitzvah in Long Island.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:03.863
(audience laughing)
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:03.863 --> 00:02:04.696
- Twenty years ago.
- You know what though,

00:02:04.696 --> 00:02:05.670
it all builds character.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.596
That's what I'm saying.

00:02:06.596 --> 00:02:07.429
- It does.
- All the jobs.

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:08.262
I feel like it does.

00:02:08.262 --> 00:02:09.870
And humility.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.730
But what do you remember
about the first time

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.900
like you were ever like on stage,

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.860
like in a musical?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.693
- Oh, I-

00:02:14.693 --> 00:02:15.526
- [Kelly] Like your favorite one.

00:02:15.526 --> 00:02:17.850
- I had the most amazing

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.110
dosage of musical theater

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:19.943
at a young age.

00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:22.440
Because I had an amazing
elementary school music teacher

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.670
Barbara Ames.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.690
Shout out to Barbara Ames.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.120
- Get it Barbara Ames (audience cheering)

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.650
- She's actually in Tick Tick Boom.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.016
I put her in the movie.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:30.960
- Oh, I love that.
- And she plays

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.430
Jonathan Larson's music teacher.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.140
In the movie.
- I love that.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.040
- I had to, I had to-

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.060
- I know but that's so great.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.770
Like a little nugget so
everybody knows that.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:38.754
Like while watching it.

00:02:38.754 --> 00:02:39.587
- Yeah, yeah.
- That's so cool.

00:02:39.587 --> 00:02:41.310
And so she would do something

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.360
called the sixth grade play.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:43.770
She would music direct

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.240
and direct the sixth grade play.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.470
And when I was in kindergarten

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.460
it was West Side Story.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.600
And the whole school watched it.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.620
And when I was in first grade,

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.610
it was Fiddler on the Roof.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.050
And so by the time you're in fifth grade,

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:52.883
you're like,

00:02:52.883 --> 00:02:54.780
"What's our sixth grade play gonna be?"

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.550
- [Kelly] Oh my God.
- And by the time

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.540
we got to sixth grade.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.892
They ran out of age appropriate musicals

00:02:59.892 --> 00:03:00.725
(audience laughs) for 12 year olds.

00:03:00.725 --> 00:03:02.010
- Ah.
- So we did

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.360
a very unauthorized,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.090
previous six years worth of musicals.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.740
Like 20 minute versions.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.091
So when I was 12 years old-

00:03:09.091 --> 00:03:10.040
- Wait, you just picked the best songs.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.890
- We just, yeah.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.723
They did like, yeah.

00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:12.637
They just picked the
best songs and were like,

00:03:12.637 --> 00:03:14.040
"Here's a 20 minute Fiddler.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.331
Here's a 20 minute West Side-
- It's like a variety show

00:03:15.331 --> 00:03:16.164
of musicals I love it.

00:03:16.164 --> 00:03:17.070
- It was four hours long.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.270
- Oh
- Our poor parents.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.103
- my God.
- [Lin] But.

00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:21.240
All those parents hated
all of you (Kelly laughs)

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.260
- Hated us.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.260
On our wooden chairs in our auditorium.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.600
But I played a farmer in Oklahoma.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.560
Captain Hook.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.941
Bernardo in West Side Story.

00:03:29.941 --> 00:03:30.774
- [Kelly] What?

00:03:30.774 --> 00:03:32.853
- An Addaperle backup in The Wiz.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.760
And who else?

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.530
A son in Fiddler.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.220
It was like just the most
amazing experience of my life.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.053
And when you're-

00:03:42.053 --> 00:03:42.886
- [Kelly] What a boot camp.

00:03:42.886 --> 00:03:43.719
- When you're 12

00:03:43.719 --> 00:03:44.670
and you play Conrad Birdie.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.570
And you sing,

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.040
and all the girls and boys

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.780
have to faint when you sing.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.276
I was like, "I'm doing this."

00:03:50.276 --> 00:03:51.429
- [Kelly] I'm amazing.
- I'm doing this.

00:03:51.429 --> 00:03:52.694
- I'm amazing.
- For the rest of my life.

00:03:52.694 --> 00:03:53.533
(everyone laughs)

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.660
That's it, I'm done.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.530
- I love that.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.363
- Yeah.

00:03:56.363 --> 00:03:57.960
- Well that's a lot to like ask-

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.265
That's a high bar to ask of sixth graders.

00:04:00.265 --> 00:04:01.500
- [Lin] Yeah, I don't remember
- I like her, Barbara.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.060
- any math from sixth grade.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.500
I remember the sixth grade play.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.580
- I only remember FOIL.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.110
That's it for math.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.700
So anyway, you are a substitute teacher.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:09.742
I didn't know that as well.

00:04:09.742 --> 00:04:10.575
For some reason

00:04:10.575 --> 00:04:11.408
I missed that.
- Yeah my first job

00:04:11.408 --> 00:04:13.800
out of college was teaching
seventh grade English

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.206
at my old high school.

00:04:15.206 --> 00:04:16.039
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:04:16.039 --> 00:04:18.150
(audience clapping)
- Yeah, it was amazing.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.070
- What was like your
favorite thing to teach?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.020
- My favorite thing to
teach was Shakespeare.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.370
We would teach A Midsummer Night's Dream.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.630
- And they were into it?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.000
- Yeah, because the thing is...

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.410
Shakespeare's really boring

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.640
when you have to read it.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.990
But if you have to act it.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.069
It's like the best.

00:04:32.069 --> 00:04:33.085
- Oh, you were a cool teacher.

00:04:33.085 --> 00:04:34.077
Yeah, yeah.
- I was kind of a cool teacher

00:04:34.077 --> 00:04:35.640
and I would, I had, you know.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.960
Everyone would pick their names out

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.830
who they were playing that day.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.760
And girls play boys

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:39.803
and boys play girls.
- Oh, see that's fun.

00:04:39.803 --> 00:04:40.636
You act it out.

00:04:40.636 --> 00:04:42.000
- And in acting it out, you understand it.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.860
- It's like English/Drama class.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:44.693
I like it.
- Yeah.

00:04:44.693 --> 00:04:45.600
It was really, it was really fun.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.030
And I, you know they
offered me a full-time job

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:48.863
and I could-

00:04:48.863 --> 00:04:49.710
And I loved it.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:50.970
I truly loved teaching.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.230
And so I could see

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.280
the Mr. Holland's Opus

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.257
version of my life of like-

00:04:54.257 --> 00:04:55.090
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.220
- I'll be here 30 years

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.330
and I'll inspire a lot of kids.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.100
And I'll never finish my play.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.600
And so I ran.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.137
And so I basically was like,

00:05:02.137 --> 00:05:03.360
"I can't teach full time.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.980
I'm writing the show In the Heights."

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.210
So I was a professional

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:07.680
substitute teacher (audience clapping)

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.513
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:05:08.513 --> 00:05:11.280
- I was basically a sub
at my old high school.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.537
Until In the Heights opened.

00:05:12.537 --> 00:05:13.890
- But you bet on yourself.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:14.723
You bet on yourself.

00:05:14.723 --> 00:05:15.556
- [Lin] I did, I did.
- And your dream, that's cool.

00:05:15.556 --> 00:05:18.210
- And weirdly my future brother-in-law

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.640
was one of my students.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:21.473
- What?

00:05:21.473 --> 00:05:23.760
Your life is weird.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.690
Wait, what?

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.570
- Yeah, he was still a junior

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.950
when I was subbing.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:32.040
And then when I started dating my wife.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.577
He turns to his sister and goes,

00:05:33.577 --> 00:05:35.940
"You're dating Mr. Miranda?

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:36.975
From school?"

00:05:36.975 --> 00:05:38.340
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.770
And now he's my brother.
- I love that.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:40.945
(everyone laughs)

00:05:40.945 --> 00:05:42.333
Oh my god.

00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:43.893
What a small world.
- Yeah.

